1. Health check — GET /health

curl -i "https://auth-service-red.vercel.app/health"
2. Signup — POST /api/auth/signup

curl -i -X POST "https://auth-service-red.vercel.app/api/auth/signup" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email":"user@example.com","password":"secret123"}'
3. Login — POST /api/auth/login (returns a token)

curl -i -X POST "https://auth-service-red.vercel.app/api/auth/login" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email":"user@example.com","password":"secret123"}'
Capture the token automatically for the protected routes below (needs jq):

TOKEN=$(curl -s -X POST "https://auth-service-red.vercel.app/api/auth/login" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"email":"user@example.com","password":"secret123"}' | jq -r '.token')
echo "$TOKEN"
4. Get current user — GET /api/auth/me (protected)

curl -i "https://auth-service-red.vercel.app/api/auth/me" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
5. Verify token — GET /api/auth/verify (protected)

curl -i "https://auth-service-red.vercel.app/api/auth/verify" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
6. Logout — POST /api/auth/logout (protected)

curl -i -X POST "https://auth-service-red.vercel.app/api/auth/logout" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
